cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code in your research, please cite it using this metadata."
type: dataset
title: "EthioSwitch-Bench: A Benchmark for LLM Evaluation on English-Amharic Code-Switching"
abstract: >
  EthioSwitch-Bench is the first large-scale, human-validated benchmark for evaluating
  Large Language Model performance on English-Amharic code-switching in multi-turn
  conversational dialogue. The benchmark provides two tiers: a gold-standard set of
  30 hand-crafted dialogues (v2.0) and a full benchmark corpus of 2,000 dialogues (v3.0)
  spanning 15 topics with controlled code-switch frequency and language dominance.
  All dialogues include human annotations for coherence, semantic consistency,
  switch-point naturalness, fluency, and inter-annotator agreement (Cohen's kappa).
